  "prefLabel": "Fam 701.02 Duration of Certification",
  "priorExpiration": "2018-10-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fam 701.02 Duration of Certification. Renewed certification of a training program issued pursuant to this chapter shall be valid for a period of 3 years unless earlier terminated by the board for:\n\n(a) Failure of the program to maintain the program components and standards described in Fam 604;\n\n(b) Failure of the program to comply with the ongoing requirements set forth in Fam 706;\n\n(c) Failure of the program to have as a director an individual meeting the requirements of Fam 604.09;\n\n(d) Suspension of the family mediator certification of the director;\n\n(e) Violation of Fam 500 by the director or members of the training staff;\n\n(f) Fraud or deceit in obtaining or attempting to obtain certification; or\n\n(g) Violation by the program, the director, or a member of the training staff of federal or state law prohibiting discrimination or other applicable federal or state law.\n\nSource. #9156, eff 5-10-08; ss by #9676, eff 4-2-10; ss by #12507, INTERIM, eff 4-2-18, EXPIRED: 10-1-18\n\nNew. #12638, eff 10-2-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fam100-800.html"
